        "dimension": "coverage",
        "findings": [
          {
            "dimension": "coverage",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts:1",
            "message": "The plan promises an integration-level test 'Affected native and ordinary provider regressions and build pass,' but no test title or reportedTests entry in the grounding corresponds to it. The 5 test files in the record and the 4 build tasks (t1-t4) all show passing/pass, which is consistent with this promise in substance, but there is no discrete test artifact mapped to this name, so it cannot be confirmed as a distinct executed check.",
            "expectationRef": "Affected native and ordinary provider regressions and build pass",
            "confidence": "breach",
            "findingKind": "promised-test"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "dimension": "quality",
        "findings": [
          {
            "dimension": "quality",
            "severity": "MED",
            "location": "src/daemon/review-investigation-canaries.ts",
            "message": "createProbeCanaries is a single routine that owns six nested closures (put, command, hook, activate, signals, assertCurrent) each mutating shared local state (digest freezing, private-file writes, shell command construction, hook wiring, phase activation, signal parsing). Mixing these distinct responsibilities as closures inside one function instead of named top-level helpers makes the control flow hard to follow and easy to break when one responsibility changes without the others being re-checked.",
            "counterpartRef": "",
            "confidence": "observation"
          },
          {
            "dimension": "quality",
            "severity": "MED",
            "location": "src/agent/providers/native-investigation-probe.ts",
            "message": "runNativeInvestigationProbe inlines four local closures (check, controlCost, admit, expected) on top of ~14 direct callees spanning budget admission, image/catalog verification, environment setup, and session launch. This orchestrator does too many unrelated things in one scope, which raises the chance that a change to one concern (e.g. budget admission) silently breaks another (e.g. image-pinning checks) without a corresponding test catching it.",
            "counterpartRef": "",
            "confidence": "observation"
          },
          {
            "dimension": "quality",
            "severity": "MED",
            "location": "src/agent/providers/claude-investigation-session.ts",
            "message": "claudeInvestigationArgs/claudeInvestigationControlArgs builds the claude CLI invocation args from (schema, modelArgs, cwd, indexed) independently of claudeReviewSessionArgs in cli-provider.ts, which builds claude CLI args from (schema, modelArgs) for the ordinary review-session path. Two independent arg-building functions for the same claude binary invocation risk drifting apart (e.g. one adding a new required flag the other omits) since neither calls the other.",
            "counterpartRef": "claudeReviewSessionArgs",
            "confidence": "observation"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "dimension": "diagram",
        "findings": []
      }
    ],
